_pdbx_entry_details.entry_id                   1TRZ 
_pdbx_entry_details.compound_details           
;THE CONFORMATIONS OF TWO MONOMERS ARE DIFFERENT AS THE
RESULT OF A CHANGE IN CONFORMATION OF THE FIRST EIGHT
RESIDUES OF THE B-CHAINS.  IN MONOMER I, B 1 - B 8 ADOPT
AN EXTENDED CONFORMATION WHILE IN MONOMER II THIS SEGMENT
ADOPTS AN ALPHA-HELICAL CONFORMATION, DISRUPTED AT B 3 AND
B 2.
;
_pdbx_entry_details.source_details             ? 
_pdbx_entry_details.nonpolymer_details         
;EACH OF TWO ZINC IONS IS COORDINATED BY THE THREE SYMMETRY
RELATED B 10 HIS.  THE COORDINATION SPHERE OF THE ZN1 IS
EITHER TETRAHEDRAL WITH THE FOURTH SITE FILLED BY A CL1 OR
OCTAHEDRAL, COMPLETED BY THREE SYMMETRY RELATED HOH 1.  THE
COORDINATION OF ZN2 IS TETRAHEDRAL WITH EITHER CL2 OR A
HOH 2.
;
_pdbx_entry_details.sequence_details           ? 
_pdbx_entry_details.has_ligand_of_interest     ? 
